    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.maximum_clique - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.maximum_clique.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.maximum_clique()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Find a maximum clique in the graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.maximum_clique()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Find a maximum clique in the graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.maximum_clique()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Find a maximum clique in the graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nFind a maximum clique in the graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L38230-L38340){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.maximum_clique()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Maximum clique](../assets/graphs/maximum-clique.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The same five-node graph. The triangle 2, 3, 5, in the accent color, is the largest set of nodes that are all pairwise connected. The card shows the result [2, 3, 5], size 3.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nA clique is a set of nodes in which every pair is directly connected. A maximum clique is\na largest possible clique in the graph. If multiple maximum cliques exist with the same\nsize, returns one of them (arbitrary choice). Uses the Bron-Kerbosch algorithm to\nenumerate all maximal cliques and selects the largest.\n\nNote the difference between *maximal* and *maximum*: a maximal clique cannot be extended\nby adding another node, but it need not be the largest one. `find_cliques()` returns every\nmaximal clique; this method returns only a single largest one. Use it when you want the\nmost tightly knit group in a network, for example:\n\n- the largest group of people who all know one another in a social network\n- a densely interacting core of proteins in an interaction network\n- a set of mutually compatible items (e.g., features or tasks that can all co-occur)\n\nIf you only need the size of the largest clique, `clique_number()` returns it directly.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [list[int]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Sorted list of node IDs forming a maximum clique. Empty list if graph is empty. In a\n    graph with nodes but no edges, a single node forms the largest clique, so a one-element\n    list is returned.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If called on a directed graph.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nFinding a maximum clique is $\\mathsf{NP}$-hard and, in fact, inapproximable within\nany factor of $n^{1-\\varepsilon}$ unless $\\mathsf{P} = \\mathsf{NP}$. This\nimplementation enumerates all maximal cliques via Bron-Kerbosch and returns the\nlargest, which inherits the algorithm's $O(3^{n/3})$ worst-case runtime but performs\nwell on sparse and structured inputs. If more than one maximum clique exists, one is\nreturned arbitrarily. Undirected graphs only; convert a directed graph with\n`to_undirected()` first if direction does not matter for your question.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~find_cliques`) \n\n:   List all maximal cliques.\n\n[](`~clique_number`) \n\n:   The size of a largest clique.\n\n[](`~maximum_weight_clique`) \n\n:   The clique with the largest total node weight.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\n`A`, `B`, `C` and `D` are all linked to one another, and `E` only to `A` and `B`. The\nmaximum clique is the four of them. `A`, `B` and `E` form a maximal clique too, but a\nsmaller one:\n\n::: {#2f617d32 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"A\", \"C\"), (\"A\", \"D\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"B\", \"D\"),\n     (\"C\", \"D\"), (\"E\", \"A\"), (\"E\", \"B\")]\n)\nclique = graph.maximum_clique()\n\n[graph.get_label_from_id(n) for n in clique]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n['A', 'B', 'C', 'D']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Exams that need their own slots\n\n`exams()` joins two of a made-up college's courses when some student takes both, so\ntheir exams can't share a time slot. The largest group of courses that all share\nstudents with one another is Calculus, Physics, Chemistry and Biology. Their four exams\nneed four different slots, so no timetable has fewer than four:\n\n::: {#5097b7df .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nexams = ec.exams()\nclique = exams.maximum_clique()\n\n[exams.get_label_from_id(n) for n in clique]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n['Calculus', 'Physics', 'Chemistry', 'Biology']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe six edges of the clique are its pairs of courses:\n\n::: {#d200b00b .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfrom itertools import combinations\n\nexams.plot(\n    highlight=list(combinations(clique, 2)), size_by=\"students\",\n    label_by=\"label\", seed=3, height=420,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/20